From: Lume Retro OS
Subject: [PATCH] command: network commands listen on 127.0.0.1 only

command_network_new() opens the UDP command socket (network_cmd_port, 55355)
with no host, so it listens on every interface. With a Wi-Fi network up,
anyone on that network could send commands to RetroArch (QUIT, LOAD_STATE,
...). The socket now binds to 127.0.0.1: r36os-logd, which asks GET_STATUS
through 127.0.0.1, keeps working, and no other interface reaches it.

--- a/command.c
+++ b/command.c
@@ -239,7 +239,9 @@
    command_t            *cmd = (command_t*)calloc(1, sizeof(*cmd));
    command_network_t *netcmd = (command_network_t*)calloc(
                                    1, sizeof(command_network_t));
-   int fd = socket_init((void**)&res, port, NULL,
+   /* Lume: commands from the console itself only, never from a Wi-Fi
+    * network (r36os-logd asks through 127.0.0.1) */
+   int fd = socket_init((void**)&res, port, "127.0.0.1",
          SOCKET_TYPE_DATAGRAM, AF_INET);

    RARCH_LOG("[NetCMD] %s %hu.\n",
